    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_paper_was_written_at_a_moment_when_3-2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_paper_was_written_at_a_moment_when_3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The paper was written at a moment when 3G hadn't fully rolled out, the iPhone was months away from launch, and \"app\" wasn't yet a common word. Its predictions — that cell phones would become 1-for-1 classroom devices, that mobile networks would reach remote regions, that GPS would become cheap enough to put in every student's pocket — all came true. The products the paper called for did not."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_paper_was_written_at_a_moment_when_3-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "El documento fue escrito en un momento en el que aún no había llegado la tecnología 3G, el iPhone estaba a meses de lanzarse y \"app\" todavía no era una palabra común. Sus predicciones -que los teléfonos celulares se convertirían en dispositivos de clase única para el aula, que las redes móviles llegarían a regiones remotas y que el GPS sería lo suficientemente barato como para ponerlo en la bolsa de todos los estudiantes- se cumplieron. Los productos que el documento solicitaba no existieron.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_paper_was_written_at_a_moment_when_3-2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_paper_was_written_at_a_moment_when_3"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.if_students_follow_their_curiosity_throu-2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.if_students_follow_their_curiosity_throu",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "If students follow their curiosity through real places, learning about arches, barrels, and celestial navigation because they're standing near a cathedral or a harbour, how do you assess what they've learned in a way that satisfies curriculum requirements? How do you produce the spreadsheet of numbers the principal wants while also honouring the complexity of what the student actually understood?"
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.if_students_follow_their_curiosity_throu-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "¿Cómo evalúas qué han aprendido los estudiantes si siguen su curiosidad a través de lugares reales, aprendiendo sobre arcos, barriles y navegación celeste porque están cerca de una catedral o un puerto? ¿Cómo produces la hoja de cálculo de números que el director quiere mientras también honras la complejidad de lo que realmente entendieron los estudiantes?",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.if_students_follow_their_curiosity_throu-2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.if_students_follow_their_curiosity_throu"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_document_left_that_question_open_the-2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_document_left_that_question_open_the",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The document left that question open. The school system didn't solve it either. For nearly two decades, \"outdoor learning\" remained either a vague aspiration or a logistical nightmare — teachers with clipboards, activities that produced no artifact, experiences that disappeared the moment students came back inside."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_document_left_that_question_open_the-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "El documento dejó esta pregunta abierta. El sistema escolar tampoco la resolvió. Durante casi dos décadas, \"aprendizaje al aire libre\" siguió siendo una vaga aspiración o un desastre logístico -profesores con cuadernos, actividades que no produjeron ningún artefacto y experiencias que desaparecieron en el momento en que los estudiantes volvieron al interior.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_document_left_that_question_open_the-2026-06-23T07:17:52.661395+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_document_left_that_question_open_the"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_first_part_was_solved_by_smartphones-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_first_part_was_solved_by_smartphones",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The first part was solved by smartphones. Photo, audio, GPS coordinates, timestamps — a student at a creek bank can capture more evidence in ten minutes than a field trip clipboard could hold in a day. What remained was the second part: structured inquiry that didn't just document experience but deepened it."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_first_part_was_solved_by_smartphones-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "La primera parte fue resuelta por los smartphones. Foto, audio, coordenadas GPS, timestamps - un estudiante en el margen de un arroyo puede capturar más evidencia en diez minutos que una libreta de campo podría contener en un día. Lo que quedó fue la segunda parte: investigación estructurada que no solo documenta la experiencia sino que profundiza en ella.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_first_part_was_solved_by_smartphones-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_first_part_was_solved_by_smartphones"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.thats_where_peri_comes_in_peri_is_peripa-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.thats_where_peri_comes_in_peri_is_peripa",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "That's where Peri comes in. Peri is Peripateticware's AI guide — named, like the software, after the Aristotelian method. Peri doesn't answer questions. It asks them. It follows the five-phase inquiry sequence — Engage, Observe, Analyse, Explain, Apply — that Aristotle used in the Lyceum and that cognitive science has since validated as a path to genuine understanding, not just retention. Peri takes a student's observation and asks the next right question. When the student gets it right, Peri tests the implication. When the student is vague, Peri asks for evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.thats_where_peri_comes_in_peri_is_peripa-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "Esto es donde entra Peri. Peri es el guía AI de Peripateticware - nombrado, como el software, después del método aristotélico. Peri no responde a las preguntas. Pregunta. Seguir la secuencia de cinco fases de investigación - Engage, Observe, Analyze, Explain, Apply - que Aristóteles usó en el Lyceum y que la ciencia cognitiva ha validado como un camino hacia una comprensión genuina, no solo de retención.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.thats_where_peri_comes_in_peri_is_peripa-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.thats_where_peri_comes_in_peri_is_peripa"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_result_is_an_artifact_a_field_journa-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_result_is_an_artifact_a_field_journa",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The result is an artifact: a field journal entry with captures, extended analysis, and a record of the inquiry itself. Teachers can see not just what a student concluded but how they got there. Rubrics aligned to Bloom's taxonomy and standards frameworks — CCSS, NGSS, TEKS, or your own — make the assessment legible to any curriculum coordinator. The spreadsheet and the real learning finally occupy the same document."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_result_is_an_artifact_a_field_journa-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "El resultado es un artefacto: una entrada del diario de campo con capturas, análisis extendido y un registro de la investigación en sí. Los maestros pueden ver no solo lo que un estudiante concluyó sino cómo llegaron allí. Las normas alineadas a la taxonomía de Bloom y los marcos de estándares - CCSS, NGSS, TEKS o propios - hacen la evaluación legible para cualquier coordinador curricular.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_result_is_an_artifact_a_field_journa-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_result_is_an_artifact_a_field_journa"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The 2007 paper described a \"choose your own adventure\" model of learning — one where students follow tangents, pursue what interests them, and encounter core curriculum concepts through the side doors of genuine curiosity rather than the front door of instruction. The paper acknowledged this was \"somewhat chaotic\" and that it would require new kinds of instructional design, new assessment tools, and teachers willing to trade some control for authentic engagement."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "El artículo de 2007 describió un modelo \"elige tu propio camino\" de aprendizaje - uno en el que los estudiantes siguen tangencias, persiguen lo que les interesa y encuentran conceptos del currículum básico a través de las puertas laterales de la curiosidad genuina en lugar de la puerta de entrada de la instrucción. El artículo reconoció que esto era \"algo caótico\" y que requeriría nuevos tipos de diseño instruccional, nuevas herramientas de evaluación y profesores dispuestos a intercambiar algo de control por el compromiso auténtico.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_2007_paper_described_a_choose_your_o"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "Peripateticware doesn't fully solve the chaos — that tension is real and probably permanent. What it does is give teachers enough structure to stay sane (designed activities, learning targets, completion phases, teacher approval workflows) while giving students enough freedom to actually go somewhere (GPS-triggered content, student-proposed activities, self-directed field notes, peer projects)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "Peripateticware no resuelve completamente el caos - esa tensión es real y probablemente permanente. Lo que hace es dar a los maestros suficiente estructura para mantener la cordura (actividades diseñadas, objetivos de aprendizaje, fases de finalización, flujos de aprobación del profesor) mientras dan a los estudiantes suficiente libertad para realmente ir a algún lugar (contenido activado por GPS, actividades propuestas por el estudiante, anotaciones de campo autodirigidas, proyectos entre pares).",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c-2026-06-23T07:18:02.576314+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.peripateticware_doesnt_fully_solve_the_c"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_reverse_scavenger_hunt_where_student-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_reverse_scavenger_hunt_where_student",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The reverse scavenger hunt — where students propose an activity based on something they found — is the closest thing in the platform to that 2007 vision. A student finds a peculiar rock formation. They propose it as an activity. The teacher approves it. Other students go look. Questions emerge that no curriculum document anticipated. Learning moves."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_reverse_scavenger_hunt_where_student-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "La caza del tesoro al revés - donde los estudiantes proponen una actividad basada en algo que encontraron - es lo más parecido a esa visión de 2007. Un estudiante encuentra una peculiar formación rocosa. Proponen hacerla como actividad. El profesor la aprueba. Otros estudiantes van a verlo. Surgen preguntas que ningún documento del currículo anticipó. El aprendizaje se mueve.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_reverse_scavenger_hunt_where_student-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_reverse_scavenger_hunt_where_student"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The short answer is that most of the enabling technology wasn't ready in 2007. GPS in every pocket came first (2010–2015). Then high-quality mobile cameras. Then cloud APIs cheap enough for schools. Then local AI models (Ollama, llama.cpp) that can run on a teacher's home server without a $10,000/month inference bill. The 2007 paper was right about the destination; it couldn't have known how long the road would be."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "La respuesta corta es que en 2007, la mayoría de la tecnología habilitadora no estaba lista. Los GPS en cada bolsillo llegaron primero (2010-2015). Luego las cámaras móviles de alta calidad. Después las APIs en la nube baratas suficientes para las escuelas. Luego los modelos locales de IA (Ollama, llama.cpp) que pueden ejecutarse en el servidor del profesor sin una factura de inferencia de $10,000/mes. El documento de 2007 tenía razón sobre el destino; no podía saber cuánto tiempo duraría la carretera.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_short_answer_is_that_most_of_the_ena"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "The longer answer is that educational technology spent those years solving the wrong problem. EdTech iterated on the classroom — better LMS, better video, better quiz tools. It made the existing model more efficient. Peripateticware doesn't try to make the classroom more efficient. It tries to replace the classroom, at least occasionally, with the world."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "La respuesta más larga es que la tecnología educativa pasó esos años solucionando el problema equivocado. La edtech iteró en la clase - un LMS mejor, mejores videos, mejores herramientas de cuestionario. Intentaba hacer la clase existente más eficiente. Peripatético no intenta hacer la clase más eficiente. Intenta reemplazar la clase, al menos ocasionalmente, con el mundo.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.the_longer_answer_is_that_educational_te"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "@type": "prov:Activity",
      "prov:startTime": "2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00",
      "actor": {
        "@id": "agent:OLLAMA-hf.co/s3nh/Unbabel-TowerInstruct-7B-v0.1-GGUF_Q4_K_M_Profile__Technical/Legal_Documentation_|_Temp__0.1"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "That's a harder sell. Schools are risk-averse. Outdoor learning has a liability optic. \"The world is your classroom\" sounds like a marketing line until you've watched a ten-year-old explain sediment transport to a crow-shaped AI guide while standing in a creek bed, and then read the field journal entry they wrote that afternoon, and understood that they understood."
    },
    {
      "@id": "entity:target-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver-v1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "prov:value": "Eso es un vendedor más difícil. Las escuelas son cautelosas. El aprendizaje al aire libre tiene una perspectiva de responsabilidad. \"El mundo es tu aula\" suena como una línea de marketing hasta que has visto a un niño de diez años explicar el transporte sedimentario a un guía AI en forma de cuervo mientras está parado en un lecho de arroyo y luego has leído el diario de campo que escribieron esa tarde, y entendido que lo entienden.",
      "generated_by": {
        "@id": "activity:translation-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver-2026-06-23T07:18:16.016469+00:00"
      },
      "used_source": {
        "@id": "entity:source-pages_originstorypage.thats_a_harder_sell_schools_are_riskaver"
      }
    },
